      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For MyCorp, the process begins by entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening unit establishes the process start and the first action step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After entering expenses, the next step is to generate a spreadsheet."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly captures the second sequential action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "branch:b1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the spreadsheet is generated, the request can be approved or disapproved."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the first approval decision point as an XOR branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the request is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "The guard models the negative outcome ('No') and the converge node routes flow back to the start of the loop, preserving the described loopback behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the request is approved, the expenses can be paid out."
      ],
      "justification": "The positive guard ('Yes') leads directly to the payout action, matching the source arm."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "branch:b2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The process then checks again if the request is approved or not."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the explicit second approval check as a separate XOR branch, preserving the text's repeated logic."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Second negative branch guard routing back to the same converge point, faithfully repeating the loop behaviour described."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n9",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "But if it is approved, the expenses can be paid out."
      ],
      "justification": "Second positive branch guard and payout action, mirroring the first positive path as written in the source."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, after the expenses are paid out, the process comes to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Structural end node corresponding to the explicit termination statement."
    }
